ALL THREE OF README 5.2's ARMS PASS THE SAME 120 CHECKS. That is section 5.1's
binding condition on a floor that is different code from the target: identical
wire bytes at every level, checked by running the corpus on each, and a
divergence between them is a defect rather than a variant.

Arms checked for byte identity (R2):
  gp-tba    Google.Protobuf  msg.ToByteArray()                  -- what application code writes
  gp-wto    Google.Protobuf  CalculateSize + WriteTo(Span)      -- the fair encode baseline
  managed   the generated pure-C# codec, one pass, learned length width
  2pass     the same codec, SizeOf then WriteSized              -- Google.Protobuf's shape
  vector    the committed .bin, byte for byte (payloads at or under 64 KB)
  mrt/grt   decode then re-encode reproduces the canonical bytes
  value     decode then compare FIELD BY FIELD against the graph the builder made,
            through a comparer emitted from the same walker as the codec. Without
            this column a decoder that drops a field the encoder also omits passes.

The core-ffi arm is absent by instruction: ABI v1 open decision 1 is unsettled,
so the ABI is not frozen and a binding built against a draft measures the draft.

